## 12. Final Outcome

The final Botsho Geotechnical Engineers network successfully demonstrates:

- VLSM subnetting of the assigned `172.30.42.0/23` block
- Four functional VLANs
- IEEE 802.1Q trunking
- Router-on-a-stick inter-VLAN routing
- Scoped multi-VLAN DHCP
- Static printer and server addressing
- Shared printer access from both departments
- Inter-VLAN communication
- Server reachability
- Successful end-to-end network verification

The completed project progressed from client requirements and network design to Packet Tracer implementation and final verification.

---

## 13. Milestone 3 Conclusion

The final implementation satisfies the major networking requirements demonstrated within the project scope.

Engineering and Administration receive addresses from their correct DHCP scopes, while the shared printer and server remain at predictable static addresses.

CR8 is satisfied because both departmental VLANs can successfully reach the shared printer in VLAN 30.

The completed testing confirms that the VLAN, trunking, DHCP, addressing, and routing configurations operate together successfully.
